<title>CHILE: CHILE FOREX RESERVES FALL $109 MLN IN JULY.</title>
<headline>CHILE FOREX RESERVES FALL $109 MLN IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's international reserves fell $109 million in July to total $17.49 billion on July 31, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The report did not give any reason for the drop.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
